.Dd June 9, 2026
.Dt MBT_CONN 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mbt_conn_new ,
.Nm mbt_conn_read ,
.Nm mbt_conn_write ,
.Nm mbt_conn_available ,
.Nm mbt_conn_set_watermark ,
.Nm mbt_conn_peer_addr ,
.Nm mbt_conn_free
.Nd buffered bidirectional connection with watermark callbacks
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In mbt/conn.h
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_conn_new "struct mbt_ev *ev" "struct mbt_conn **out" "int fd" "mbt_conn_read_cb readcb" "mbt_conn_event_cb eventcb" "void *arg"
.Ft ssize_t
.Fn mbt_conn_read "struct mbt_conn *c" "void *buf" "size_t len"
.Ft ssize_t
.Fn mbt_conn_write "struct mbt_conn *c" "const void *buf" "size_t len"
.Ft size_t
.Fn mbt_conn_available "struct mbt_conn *c"
.Ft void
.Fn mbt_conn_set_watermark "struct mbt_conn *c" "size_t low"
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_conn_peer_addr "struct mbt_conn *c" "char *buf" "size_t buflen" "uint16_t *port"
.Ft void
.Fn mbt_conn_free "struct mbt_conn *c"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A connection wraps a socket fd in a buffered stream with watermark-based read callbacks.

.Pp
Fn mbt_conn_new
takes ownership of
Fa fd .
When enough data has arrived and hits the low watermark threshold set via
Fn mbt_conn_set_watermark ,
the read callback fires so the caller can drain it.
.Fn mbt_conn_available
returns how many bytes are readable without blocking;
.Fn mbt_conn_read
drains them into
Fa buf .

.Pp
Fn mbt_conn_write
pushes data toward the peer asynchronously (never blocks the event loop).
Return value indicates how many bytes were staged for transmission.
.Fn mbt_conn_peer_addr
resolves and returns the remote address string plus port via getpeername().
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Functions returning
.Ft int
or
.Ft ssize_t
return 0 on success or a negative errno value on failure.
.Pp
.Fn mbt_conn_set_callbacks
replaces the read and event callbacks on an existing connection.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mbt_event 3 ,
.Xr mbt_peer 3
